@title Welcome to Bayside Community Pantry
@subtitle A short guide for new volunteers
@author Rosa Delgado, Volunteer Coordinator

We are so glad you are here. This page tells you what you need to know before your first shift.

## Hours

table = Day,Distribution hours; Tuesday,9:00 to 12:00; Thursday,16:00 to 19:00; Saturday,8:00 to 12:00

Come to as many shifts as you like.

Before your first shift, please join our 45-minute orientation. It runs at 8:00 on the first Saturday of each month.

! The next orientation is on Saturday 2026-11-07 at 8:00.

## Your first shift

- [ ] Arrive 15 minutes early.
- [ ] Check in with the shift lead. Look for the green apron.
- [ ] Wear closed-toe shoes.
- [ ] Leave your valuables in the locker.

!! Please do not lift more than 25 pounds on your own. Ask someone to help.

Our clients are our neighbors. We do not ask about their income, and we do not take photos.

## Roles

You may be asked to help with any of these:
- Sorting donations
- Stocking shelves
- Packing family boxes
- Greeting clients at the door
- Helping carry boxes to cars

## Getting here

- **Parking** is behind the building on Harbor Street.
- **By bus,** take route 14. The stop is across the road.

! Can't make a shift? Text 555-0142 at least 24 hours ahead, so we can find cover.

## Thank you

Last year, our volunteers made a real difference.

kpi Volunteers | 312 | last year
kpi Hours given | 9,400 | last year
kpi Meals a month | 41,000 | on average

Every one of those hours mattered. Thank you for joining them.
